Bundled software
----------------

The platform packages (win32-x64, darwin-arm64, darwin-x64) also carry a
simulator runtime, runtime/runtime.tar.gz, made of separate programs under
their own licenses. Their license texts and sources are listed inside it:

- V5 Simulacrum, the simulator (runtime/sim/): LGPL-3.0-or-later, with
  exceptions per directory (runtime/sim/NOTICE, LICENSE, COPYING,
  THIRD_PARTY.md).
  Source: https://github.com/UNSW-Robotics-Competition-Club/v5-simulacrum
- QEMU with the VEX device models (runtime/qemu/bin/qemu-system-arm):
  GPL-2.0-or-later. runtime/QEMU-SOURCE.txt names the QEMU release and the
  v5-simulacrum commit it was built from.
- glib, pixman and their dependencies (runtime/qemu/lib/): their own
  licenses (LGPL, MIT).
- CPython from python-build-standalone (runtime/python/): the Python
  Software Foundation License (runtime/python/lib/python3.12/LICENSE.txt).

VEX's firmware (VEXos) is not part of this package: the extension downloads
it from VEX on first start.
